## Proposed PO Review Schema

**Task title:** Purchase Order Review

**What the reviewer sees (read-only):**

| Field | Label | Type |
|---|---|---|
| `ponumber` | PO Number | string |
| `vendorname` | Vendor Name | string |
| `totalamount` | Total Amount | number |

**What the reviewer fills in:**

| Field | Label | Type | Required |
|---|---|---|---|
| `notes` | Notes | string | No |

**Action buttons:**

| Button | Role | What happens |
|---|---|---|
| ✅ **Approve** | Primary | Flow continues → logs the approval |
| ❌ **Reject** | Secondary | Flow ends immediately — nothing further runs |

---

**A note on PO data:** Since this is a fresh flow with no upstream data source yet, the PO Number, Vendor Name, and Total Amount will be passed in as flow-level input variables when the flow is triggered. You'd call this flow from whatever system hands you the PO (e.g. an RPA bot, a form submission, a scheduled job).

**After approval:** a script node will log `"PO <number> approved"` — you can swap this out for a real system call (SAP, a database write, etc.) later.

---

