## What was built

**Solution:** `POReview/POReview.uipx`
**Flow file:** `POReview/POReview/POReview.flow`

### Nodes inserted (left → right)

| # | Node ID | Type | What it does |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `start` | Manual trigger | Kicks off the flow when you hit Run |
| 2 | `fetchPO1` | Script | Returns hardcoded PO data — `PO-2026-0042`, `Acme Supplies Ltd.`, `$12,450.00` |
| 3 | `poReview1` | **QuickForm HITL** | Creates an Action Center task for you to review the PO |
| 4 | `logApproval1` | Script | Logs `"PO PO-2026-0042 approved"` — only runs if you click Approve |

### HITL task schema

| Field | Shows in form as | Direction |
|---|---|---|
| PO Number | `PO-2026-0042` (read-only) | input |
| Vendor Name | `Acme Supplies Ltd.` (read-only) | input |
| Total Amount | `12450` (read-only) | input |
| Notes | Empty text box (optional, editable) | output |

**Buttons:** ✅ Approve (primary — continues to log node) · ❌ Reject (ends flow immediately)

### Edges wired

```
start ──output──▶ fetchPO1 ──success──▶ poReview1 ──completed──▶ logApproval1
```

The `Reject` outcome has `action: "End"` — the flow terminates right there, no log node runs.

### Runtime variables (for downstream scripts)
| Variable | Contains |
|---|---|
| `$vars.poReview1.output.notes` | Whatever you typed in the Notes box |
| `$vars.poReview1.status` | `"Approve"` or `"Reject"` |

---

**When you're ready to go live**, just swap `fetchPO1`'s hardcoded return for a real HTTP call or database lookup — the rest of the flow stays exactly as-is. You can pack and publish with:

```bash
cd POReview
uip solution pack . ./out
uip solution publish ./out/*.zip
```

